BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:African American Women in Cambridge Walking Tour
DTSTART:20240109T000000
DTEND:20240109T020000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:f4a39b059734fd6578704176e60d56@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:This tour provides an opportunity to visit and interact with t
 he spaces that influential Black women in Cambridge inhabited during the 1
 9th century. These historical figures include Harriet Jacobs\, Charlotte H
 awkins Brown\, Alberta V. Scott\, Pauline Hopkins\, Maria Baldwin\, Mary W
 alker and more! The walking tour is a partnership between a History Depart
 ment course at Harvard College and the Cambridge Black History Project.\n
 \nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/afric
 an-american-women-in-cambridge-walking-tour/78986/
LOCATION:Cambridge\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02139
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/african-american-women-in-cambridge-w
 alking-tour/78986/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cambridge Black Trailblazer Bookmarks
DTSTART:20240109T000000
DTEND:20240109T020000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:015dec0fc634bf84813c5544902667@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Biographies of 23 Trailblazers have been published as bookmark
 s and distributed to all Cambridge public school libraries and to all Camb
 ridge Public Library branches. This project offers young readers free book
 marks featuring images on the front and biographies on the back. The goal 
 is to familiarize a broader audience with a cohort of pioneering black ind
 ividuals who have yet to be commemorated with physical landmarks in the ci
 ty. Stop by the Cambridge Public Library to pick up your free bookmarks an
 d learn more about these Cambridge Trailblazers!\n\nSources: Meet Boston\n
 Event page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/cambridge-black-trailblazer-b
 ookmarks/78987/
LOCATION:Cambridge\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/cambridge-black-trailblazer-bookmarks
 /78987/
END:VEVENT
