BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tastings at Plymouth Bay Winery
DTSTART:20250205T000000
DTEND:20250205T020000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:1ff702ef396ca913badbbfd52cb54a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:We love nothing more than introducing our collection to newcom
 ers\, and welcoming returning guests. Tasting Options Reservations can be 
 made but we also welcome spontaneous drop-ins for our tasting options. Sea
 tings are limited to 60 minutes. Larger groups (8 or more guests)\, may be
  extended to 90 minutes provided a reservation has been made. A $50 deposi
 t is requested for group (8 or more guests) reservations. Guests with rese
 rvations will be seated first. All other guests will be seated on a first 
 come\, first served basis. Your tasting includes five wines in the form of
  a curated flight for $15.00**\, or $20.00 to try all available core wines
  plus your choice of an available seasonal wine. You may try additional wi
 nes for $1.00** per taste. Limited Series Varietals are not available to t
 aste. Take home an etched\, commemorative glass as a memory of your experi
 ence! Individual cheese plates are available for an additional $6.00** per
  person. We offer cheese or hummus\, crackers and fresh fruit*. Gluten fre
 e crackers are available. Charcuterie Boards are available for $18.00. Add
  $2.00 for a sweet treat! *Subject to change based on availability of the 
 freshest ingredients. January - March Friday - Saturday 12-5:00PM (last se
 ating 4:15) Sunday 12-4:00PM (last seating 3:15) April - December Monday -
  Friday 12-5:00PM (last seating 4:15) Saturday 12-5:30PM (last seating 4:3
 0) Sunday 12-4:00PM (last seating 3:15)\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent pag
 e: https://www.meetboston.com/event/tastings-at-plymouth-bay-winery/84036/
LOCATION:Plymouth Bay Winery\, 114 Water Street (Rear Building)\, Plymouth
 \, MA\, 02360
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/tastings-at-plymouth-bay-winery/84036
 /
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How Do You See the World?® Experience + Mapparium® Globe
DTSTART:20250207T000000
DTEND:20250207T020000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:bb10637f6233d20058becfafc084d1@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The How Do You See the World? experience features compelling s
 tories about global progress—how individuals worldwide have overcome cha
 llenges and found hope. Located on the Christian Science Plaza\, the space
  encourages you to reflect on this question while exploring the interactiv
 e exhibits. The three-story Mapparium globe—one of Boston's most well kn
 own landmarks—shows the world at one moment in time—1935. A short narr
 ation lets you consider the world before World War II from an entirely dif
 ferent perspective—from the inside of the world looking out. (Will requi
 re a timed ticket and paid admission – adults $6\, youth 0-17 free.) Lea
 ving this magnificent space\, you encounter “Our World: Mapping Progress
 \,” an exhibit which highlights humanity’s advancement since 1935 and 
 inspires hope for the future. “Points of Progress” invites you to expl
 ore a rolling record of significant events in human rights\, scientific br
 eakthroughs\, exploration\, and other fields through the post-war decades.
  For profiles of the people around the world making a difference in their 
 communities\, eight sets of interactive stories come from the pages of The
  Christian Science Monitor \, a Pulitzer Prize-winning\, international new
 spaper headquartered here and publishing daily and weekly editions since 1
 908. The Monitor was founded by Mary Baker Eddy with the object to “inju
 re no man\, but to bless all mankind.” You can learn more about Mary Bak
 er Eddy (1821-1910)\, who founded the Monitor and the Christian Science ch
 urch\, through exploring Eddy’s lifelong love of the Bible and its ongoi
 ng relevance and application to universal questions today in two more exhi
 bits. You can even explore virtual\, original materials from The Mary Bake
 r Eddy Library that document her life and the church she founded in one of
  these two exhibits.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meet
 boston.com/event/how-do-you-see-the-world%3f%c2%ae-experience-%2b-mappariu
 m%c2%ae-globe/71284/
LOCATION:The First Church of Christ\, Scientist\, 210 Massachusetts Avenue
 \, Boston\, MA\, 02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/how-do-you-see-the-world%3f%c2%ae-exp
 erience-%2b-mapparium%c2%ae-globe/71284/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
