BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boston: Votes for Women History Tour of Back Bay
DTSTART:20250815T000000
DTEND:20250815T020000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:eb6b3ec3cb28930ab233e89615803f@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Boston’s leading role in the American fight for women’s su
 ffrage is found on the tree-lined streets of its elegant Back Bay neighbor
 hood. This masterpiece of Victorian-era architecture is best experienced o
 n foot\, in a small group\, with a local guide! Your 2.5-hour tour travels
  from Boston Common into historic Back Bay\, visiting must-see landmarks s
 uch as the Public Garden\, Newbury Street\, and iconic Copley Square. Our 
 walking tour delves deeply into the years 1870 to 1920\, tumultuous decade
 s culminating in women earning the right to vote in the United States. Wal
 k in the footsteps of prolific activists and financiers\, visiting the pol
 itical battleground for pro- and anti-suffrage groups. With a captivating 
 storytelling approach\, Hub Town Tours provides the perfect introduction t
 o Boston's role in the advancement of women’s rights. As we travel past 
 key landmarks and historic homes\, your guide shares captivating stories o
 f the Bostonians who assembled the Women’s Suffrage Movement. Meet Your 
 Guide: Make Way for Ducklings\, Boston Public Garden 4 Charles St\, 02116 
 Suffolk County Boston\, US\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://ww
 w.meetboston.com/event/boston%3a-votes-for-women-history-tour-of-back-bay/
 79918/
LOCATION:Hub Town Tours\, Beacon Street at Charles Street\, Boston\, MA\, 
 02108
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston%3a-votes-for-women-history-tou
 r-of-back-bay/79918/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boston: Freedom Trail Insiders Tour with Museum Entry
DTSTART:20250816T000000
DTEND:20250816T020000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:a9a6c8de2a0eae800a1845d9cf1906@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Boston's principal role in launching the American Revolution i
 s linked by the brick-lined Freedom Trail. This world-famous pedestrian pa
 th is best experienced on foot with an expert historian. Awarded “Best o
 f Boston” by The Boston Globe \, Hub Town Tours partners with local inst
 itutions to provide unparalleled Freedom Trail experiences! Insiders Tour 
 covers Boston history inside and out\, traveling past iconic landmarks wit
 h a local historian and venturing inside two essential museums. Travel thr
 ough the heart of Downtown Boston\, visiting 11 of 16 official landmarks o
 n the Freedom Trail. Along the way\, your expert guide delves deeply into 
 the years 1768 to 1775\, the tumultuous years leading into the American Re
 volution. Step inside the very rooms where history happened as you walk in
  the footsteps of Colonial Bostonians\, all of whom grappled with the diff
 icult—yet essential—question of loyalty or rebellion to crown and coun
 try. Our Insider Tour experience includes paid admission to the Old State 
 House (1713) and Old South Meeting House (1729)\, two of Boston's most sig
 nificant landmarks. Witness where the Boston Massacre took place\, the Bos
 ton Tea Party began\, and the Declaration of Independence was first read t
 o a raucous crowd of Bostonians! Meet your guide at 121 South Market St. a
 t Faneuil Hall Marketplace. Look for the large\, red Coach banners on the 
 side of the South Market building!\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: ht
 tps://www.meetboston.com/event/boston%3a-freedom-trail-insiders-tour-with-
 museum-entry/86729/
LOCATION:Faneuil Hall Marketplace\, Faneuil Hall Marketplace 121 South Mar
 ket Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02109
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston%3a-freedom-trail-insiders-tour
 -with-museum-entry/86729/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boston: Underground Railroad History Tour of Beacon Hill
DTSTART:20250817T000000
DTEND:20250817T020000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:94c038d94d2366195121eb581933f4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Explore hidden history on Beacon Hill's Black Heritage Trail\,
  learning stories from America's "Second Revolution" prior to the U.S. Civ
 il War. Boston's role in the fight to end legalized slavery is linked by t
 he Black Heritage Trail in historic Beacon Hill. This pedestrian path is b
 est experienced on foot\, in a small group\, with a knowledgeable local gu
 ide! Your 2.5-hour loop tour travels from Boston Common to visit Undergrou
 nd Railroad sites\, elite homes of "Boston Brahmins\," and abolitionist la
 ndmarks such as the African Meeting House. Our small-group walking tour de
 lves deeply into the years 1833 to 1863\, the tumultuous years leading tow
 ard Civil War. We walk in the footsteps of 19th-century Bostonians\, all o
 f whom grappled with the "peculiar institution" of racial enslavement in t
 he U.S. With a captivating storytelling approach\, Hub Town Tours provides
  the perfect introduction to Boston's role in America's "Second Revolution
 ." As we travel past landmarks from Civil War Boston\, your guide shares t
 he gripping story of local Bostonians finding their voices and demanding a
 n end to injustice across their young nation. Meet Your Guide: The tour ga
 thers on Boston Common at the Soldiers & Sailors Monument\, just behind th
 e Boston Common Visitor Center. Looks for the tall white granite column at
 op the highest point in the park.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: htt
 ps://www.meetboston.com/event/boston%3a-underground-railroad-history-tour-
 of-beacon-hill/79893/
LOCATION:Hub Town Tours\, Soldiers & Sailors Monument Boston Common\, Bost
 on\, MA\, 02108
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston%3a-underground-railroad-histor
 y-tour-of-beacon-hill/79893/
END:VEVENT
