BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Highfield Hall & Gardens Exhibition Spotlight: New Perspectives
DTSTART:20260630T000000
DTEND:20261025T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:7912b39265b62c0430223251c167c9@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:JUNE 30th\, 2026 – OCTOBER 25th\, 2026 New Perspectives: Pai
 ntings by Deena Gu Deena Gu Laties returns to Highfield Hall & Gardens dur
 ing the summer of 2026 for her third exhibition\, The exhibit will feature
  new work by Gu in addition to examples of her work representing her early
  training in classical Chinese calligraphy. Deena is an accomplished artis
 t who melds aspects of western art with her Chinese training. Born in Shan
 ghai\, Deena Gu studied under famous Chinese painters Cheng Shifa and Tse 
 Chen-Na. She continued her art studies at the Pennsylvania Academy of Fine
  Arts when she moved to the U.S. in the 1980s\, fusing Chinese tradition w
 ith a western approach in terms of space\, color and relationship. Deena h
 as created new work for the Highfield Hall exhibit. The late renowned Phil
 adelphia artist\, Sam Maitin said\, “In painting watercolor on silk\, I 
 find that her command of the medium is extensive and eloquent. It has an i
 mperial\, regal quality. She handles it so deftly and so expertly.” Deen
 a Gu’s preferred painting medium is watercolor on silk. Silk is a tradit
 ional Chinese medium. Deena feels that the smoothness of silk exhibits the
  most exquisite colors. She also paints on rice paper as well as oils on c
 anvas. “When I paint on silk\, I feel a strong communication with its te
 xture. Silk is like a part of me\,” says Deena\, whose subjects include 
 landscapes\, flowers – especially lotus blossoms – birds\, as well as 
 portraits.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodch
 amber.org/event/highfield-hall-%26-gardens-exhibition-spotlight%3a-new-per
 spectives/52118/
LOCATION:Highfield Hall & Gardens\, 56 Highfield Drive\, Falmouth\, MA\, 0
 2540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/highfield-hall-%26-gardens-exhibi
 tion-spotlight%3a-new-perspectives/52118/
END:VEVENT
