 rum\, Photographs by George A. Taylor\, MD
DTSTART:20260901T000000
DTEND:20260930T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:a3ca3d28defd000ed315918c1d6657@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:September 1 - 30 | Sigel Gallery | Falmouth Art Center Dr. Geo
 rge Taylor’s exhibition showcases unique X-ray images of flowers and sea
  creatures. By using penetrating electromagnetic waves to “see” inside
  natural objects\, the artwork reveals hidden internal structures\, and in
 tricate geometric designs. Dr. Taylor will give a talk about his artwork o
 n Tuesday\, September 22\, at 4pm at Falmouth Art Center. The talk is free
  and open to all. The Opening Reception for this show is scheduled for Fri
 day\, September 11\, 5 – 7pm. This reception is also for two additional 
 shows Autumn Juried Exhibition featuring Petals and Palettes\, with Falmou
 th Garden Club in the Hermann Gallery\, and Upper Cape Camera Club “Amer
 ica — From Sea to Shining Sea” in the Landrau-Partan Gallery. Falmouth
  Art Center\, 137 Gifford Street\, Falmouth Free and open daily: Mon–Fri
  9am–4pm\; Sat 10am–2pm\; Sun 1–4pm Photo Credit: “Tillandsia and 
 Sea Urchins\,” a digital radiograph on Japanese washi mulberry paper\, b
 y Dr. George Taylor\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.
 capecodchamber.org/event/falmouth-art-center-presents%3a-x-ray-art%3a-usin
 g-the-invisible-spectrum-photographs-by-george-a-taylor-md/52343/
LOCATION:Falmouth Art Center\, 137 Gifford Street\, Falmouth\, MA\, 02540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/falmouth-art-center-presents%3a-x
 -ray-art%3a-using-the-invisible-spectrum-photographs-by-george-a-taylor-md
 /52343/
END:VEVENT
