BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Marathon Run Experience
DTSTART:20260908T000000
DTEND:20260908T020000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:e7901a8fb95f06422c74370a0509e7@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Ready to experience Boston from a runner's perspective? Join u
 s for this 3.6-mile guided running tour through the city's most iconic lan
 dmarks\, all while soaking in the rich history and vibrant energy that mak
 e Boston such a unique place to explore. You'll hit must-see spots—Bosto
 n Common\, the Boston Public Garden\, and Copley Square\, while passing by
  picturesque views along the Charles River Esplanade\, Beacon Hill\, and t
 he world-famous Back Bay. Along the way\, we’ll make stops at scenic spo
 ts for photo ops and quick stretch breaks—perfect for both seasoned runn
 ers and those looking to enjoy the sights at a comfortable pace. Your guid
 e will share fascinating stories about the city’s history and culture\, 
 from the moments that shaped Boston into the powerhouse it is today to the
  quirky details you won’t find in a guidebook. Whether you're a local or
  a first-time visitor\, you’ll finish this run with a deeper appreciatio
 n of Boston's charm. LEARN MORE / BOOK A TOUR\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEve
 nt page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-marathon-run-experience/8838
 6/
LOCATION:City Fit Tours\, Boston Common 139 Tremont Street\, Boston\, MA\,
  10075
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-marathon-run-experience/88386/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boston History Pub Crawl on the Freedom Trail
DTSTART:20260909T000000
DTEND:20260909T020000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:24d24ea74ae18e8d44ad910ed31141@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:History with a buzz! Join Boston Crawling for a 2-hour-and-15-
 minute history pub crawl along Boston’s famous Freedom Trail. Visit four
  iconic bars in the Faneuil Hall area while an expert local guide shares t
 he hidden\, hilarious\, and occasionally unbelievable stories of colonial 
 Boston and the American Revolution. Learn the history they left out of eig
 hth-grade social studies class\, enjoy drinks of your choice\, and meet fe
 llow travelers from around the world. This lively small-group experience i
 s a fun way for couples\, friends\, and solo travelers to explore Boston. 
 Crawls depart daily at 3:00 p.m. and 7:00 p.m.\, with an additional noon c
 rawl on Saturdays and Sundays. Meet at the Samuel Adams statue outside Fan
 euil Hall. Tours run rain\, snow\, or shine. Guests must be 21 or older an
 d present valid identification. Drinks are purchased separately\, and adva
 nce reservations are required. Cheers! LEARN MORE / BOOK A TOUR\n\nSources
 : Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston-history
 -pub-crawl-on-the-freedom-trail/93028/
LOCATION:Faneuil Hall Marketplace\, Meeting Spot: 6 Faneuil Hall Square\, 
 Boston\, MA\, 02109
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston-history-pub-crawl-on-the-freed
 om-trail/93028/
END:VEVENT
