DTEND:20260930T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:13439d856fb61dad2d4a946e2a17ea@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to tap your toes and test your musical knowledge wit
 h Music Bingo every Wednesday from 6pm to 8pm located in CanalSide Food + 
 Drink. First round starts promptly at 6:30pm. In this exciting twist on tr
 aditional bingo\, letters and numbers are replaced with song titles and ar
 tists. Players mark off songs on their bingo cards as songs are played\, c
 ompeting to win based on their music knowledge and the unpredictability of
  the game. Featuring diverse rounds of music that showcase decades\, genre
 s\, and themes\, Musical Bingo brings sing-alongs galore and an unbeatable
  blend of fun and chance—mark your card\, get five in a row\, and yell B
 INGO to claim victory! Come early to grab a bite to eat and a drink from t
 he dynamic C-Side Bar. One bingo card per person per round. Participants c
 an only win once per event date. Visit CambridgeSide.com for additional in
 formation. LEARN MORE\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.mee
 tboston.com/event/music-bingo/90362/
LOCATION:CambridgeSide\, 100 CambridgeSide Place\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02141
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/music-bingo/90362/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Naturescape Gallery presents "Cartographies of Arctic Change" by G
 reg Fiske
DTSTART:20260909T000000
DTEND:20261031T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:086251e7f93dec8555eaa1faaf1a95@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Naturescape Gallery at the Cape Cod Museum of Natural History 
 presents Cartographies of Arctic Change by Greg Fiske\, Director of Geospa
 tial Technology at Woodwell Climate Research Center in Woods Hole\, Septem
 ber through October 2026\, during Museum hours. Maps are essential to tell
 ing the story of our changing world. Cartographer Greg Fiske combines scie
 nce and art to create some of the most spectacular images of our home\, pl
 anet Earth. In this medium of cartography\, Greg’s work gives a birds-ey
 e view of our world that bridges the gap between facts and emotions\, not 
 only helping the general public to understand complex information about th
 e impact of climate change but also assist climate scientists with the cru
 cial visual information to address ways to combat it. In his time at the W
 oodwell Climate Center\, Fiske and his colleague Christina Shintani\, have
  worked on maps detailing forest carbon in the United States\, global drou
 ght forecasts\, fire detections in the Amazon Rainforest\, and Arctic comm
 unities located on permafrost ground. According to Fiske\, “cartography 
 isn’t one profession\, it’s a collection of professions”. A modern c
 artographer is a data analyst\, a statistician\, a designer\, a programmer
 \, a storyteller\, all rolled into one. Skills from each profession\, and 
 a healthy curiosity about a hundred other subjects\, are required to creat
 e maps that are informative\, attention-grabbing\, and intuitive to read. 
 Fiske began his journey into cartography via the world of computer coding 
 through his high school computer lab. With the guidance from mentors\, Gre
 g later picked up other skills\, first learning how to apply coding to geo
 spatial data and then how to display that data visually\, and as you will 
 see in his Naturescape Gallery exhibit\, make it beautiful and attention-g
 rabbing. Image Attached: River Art. This image shows elevation data from t
 he ArcticDEM project (NGA-NSF) for the Lena River delta region of north-ce
 ntral Siberia. The variations in pink shades indicate how water has change
 d the landscape through time. *On Saturday\, October 17th at 1pm join Greg
  Fiske for his program\, “Putting Science on the Map”\, an exploration
  of commonly used tools and techniques for making beautiful maps\, as well
  as the challenges\, success stories and failures\, faced in nearly two an
 d half decades of making maps for Woods Hole scientists.\n\nSources: Cape 
 Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/naturescape-
 gallery-presents-cartographies-of-arctic-change-by-greg-fiske/52220/
LOCATION:Cape Cod Museum of Natural History\, 869 Route 6A\, Brewster\, MA
 \, 02631
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/naturescape-gallery-presents-cart
 ographies-of-arctic-change-by-greg-fiske/52220/
END:VEVENT
