BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Call for Art! - America\, Beautiful\, and... a Juried Exhibition
DTSTART:20260923T000000
DTEND:20261125T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:e903315e1a13401a2e8d03eb07754d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of America’s Semi-quincentennial\, Highfield 
 Hall & Gardens invites artists to reflect on the American experience throu
 gh works that explore how America is lived\, remembered\, celebrated\, que
 stioned\, and reimagined. America\, Beautiful and…. offers an opportunit
 y to consider not only what is beautiful about America\, but also what com
 es after the “and.” Submissions via entrythingy.com (use link) through
  November 30\, 2026. Jury selection December 8\, 2026. Exhibition runs Mar
 ch 4 - May 30\, 2027. Jackie Reeves and Lauren Wolk\, named the Arts Found
 ation of Cape Cod’s 2026 Artists of the Year\, will serve as jurors for 
 the exhibition. Reeves and Wolk each approach creative expression from dif
 ferent disciplines and points of view\, offering the exhibition a thoughtf
 ul dialogue between visual art and storytelling\, Art Categories Accepted:
  Ceramics\, Collage\, Drawing\, Fiber\, Fine Art Photography\, Mixed Media
 \, Mosaic\, Oil and Acrylic Painting\, Pastel Painting\, Print Making\, Sc
 ulpture\, Printmaking (original prints using a press or other printmaking 
 process) and Watercolor. Giclees and similar prints that are copies of ori
 ginal art are not allowed. Please make sure that you submit only images th
 at accurately depict the artwork you are entering. If the submitted on-lin
 e entry is not an accurate depiction of the artwork it will be disqualifie
 d. No substitutions for the accepted artwork are allowed. Awards $200 Best
  in Show | $100 each- four judge’s awards | Four Honorable Mentions Juro
 rs Lauren Wolk is a visual artist represented by the Larkin Gallery (Harwi
 ch Port and Provincetown\, MA)\, New York Times bestselling author of seve
 ral books for young readers\, published poet\, award-winning filmmaker\, a
 nd\, with Jackie Reeves\, co-founder of The InkLine Project and the Arts F
 oundation of Cape Cod’s 2026 Artist of the Year. She lives in Centervill
 e\, MA.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamb
 er.org/event/call-for-art!-america-beautiful-and-a-juried-exhibition/52495
 /
LOCATION:Highfield Hall & Gardens\, 56 Highfield Drive\, Falmouth\, MA\, 0
 2540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/call-for-art!-america-beautiful-a
 nd-a-juried-exhibition/52495/
END:VEVENT
