DESCRIPTION:Two and a half centuries of America are commemorated by guitar
 ist Aaron Larget-Caplan in GUITAR AMERICA 250\, an exploration of the Unit
 ed States’ musical history. From The Star-Spangled Banner and America th
 e Beautiful to Paul Simon’s America and Eddie Van Halen’s 316\, Larget
 -Caplan journeys through the soundscapes of a diverse nation. The evening 
 includes music by abolitionists\, immigrants\, suffragettes\, revolutionar
 ies and rockstars with spoken word provided by special guest\, poet Richar
 d Hoffman. Admission to this concert is free but advance reservations are 
 recommended.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofbosto
 n.org/event/aaron-larget-caplan-guitar-america-250-revolutionaries-and-roc
