BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Promised Land: Jewish Patriots during the American Revolution
DTSTART:20260929T000000
DTEND:20260929T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:5764790ebbaed52f219ba8440f17a8@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:In this virtual talk\, historian Adam Jortner will show how Je
 ws played a critical role both in winning the American Revolution--fightin
 g for the Patriot cause from Bunker Hill to Yorktown--and in defining the 
 republic that was created from it. As the most visible non-Christian relig
 ion\, Judaism was central to the debate over religious freedom in America 
 at a critical juncture. During the war every city with a synagogue fell to
  the British-with the exception of Philadelphia\, birthplace to the Declar
 ation of Independence and a core of resistance. Jewish patriots throughout
  the colonies flocked to the city\, where they re-founded the local synago
 gue as a distinctively American organization. After the war\, Jews began t
 o press for full citizenship in the hope that liberty would apply to every
 one\, and that the limits to freedom imposed on Jews in the Old World woul
 d be removed in the New. Register for this virtual program here. About Ada
 m Jortner Adam Jortner is professor of American History at Auburn Universi
 ty. He has published four books on the history of American religion\, mira
 cles\, witchcraft\, and the American Revolution\, including A Promised Lan
 d: Jewish Patriots\, the American Revolution\, and the Birth of Religious 
 Freedom (2024). From 2021-2025\, he wrote regular columns for Current on h
 istory\, religion\, and current events. He is also the author and performe
 r of four Audible Original series on the history of religion\, witchcraft
 \, and monsters. His performance in “The Hidden History of the Boston Te
 a Party” was a top ten nonfiction download on Audible in January 2024. H
 e also served on the script team for the PBS show "Where in Time is Carmen
  Sandiego?" In 2026\, Jortner will present a streaming video series for Am
 erica’s 250th anniversary\, "1776: Years that Mattered." He was an AAS-A
 merican Society for Eighteenth-Century Studies Fellow in 2014-15.\n\nSourc
 es: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentra
 lma.org/event/a-promised-land%3a-jewish-patriots-during-the-american-revol
 ution/30501/
LOCATION:American Antiquarian Society\, 185 Salisbury St.\, Worcester\, MA
 \, 01609
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/a-promised-land%3a-jewish-patr
 iots-during-the-american-revolution/30501/
END:VEVENT
