DESCRIPTION:Join us on Tuesday\, September 29th at 5:15 and on the 4th Tue
 sday of each month for a new book club at the Woods Hole Library! The Crea
 tive Living Book Club meets every month with the goal of building a suppor
 tive creative community. Exploring books ranging from poetry to collage ar
 tists to essays on color to advice from other creatives\, we dive into how
  to build creative rituals into our daily lives and explore new art forms 
 and how to embrace creativity as a way of life. Feel free to bring paper t
 o doodle on\, your current fiber arts craft\, or a creative project to wor
 k on during our monthly meetings as we meet to discuss our latest read! We
  don’t want to just talk about creativity\, we want to embody it! For th
 e group’s first meeting on September 29\, participants will read and dis
 cuss essays by Audre Lorde and Katy Kelleher. You can access the materials
  here: Poetry is Not a Luxury by Audre Lorde Hue’s Hue series by Katy Ke
 lleher\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchambe
 r.org/event/creative-living-book-club-at-woods-hole-public-library/52416/
