BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jean-Luc Ponty Legacy Concert
DTSTART:20260929T000000
DTEND:20260929T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:973c8ea7e51b42452ce5f3cdd92103@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Jean-Luc Ponty Legacy Concert will celebrate the storied c
 areer of one of the most influential figures in the contemporary string wo
 rld. This concert will take place on Tuesday\, September 29th\, which coin
 cides with Jean-Luc Ponty’s 84th birthday. Featuring all-star faculty\, 
 alumni\, and students from the string department (led by Chelsey Green\, J
 ason Anick\, and Jeremy Harman)\, Berklee World Strings\, and the guitar\,
  piano\, percussion\, and bass departments\, this concert will highlight t
 he extensive and profound career of a true jazz legend. Special Guest Alum
 ni Mads Tolling on violin. With special guest Mads Tolling\, an internatio
 nally renowned violinist and composer from Copenhagen\, Denmark\, now base
 d in San Francisco. A former nine-year member of both bassist Stanley Clar
 ke's band and the celebrated Turtle Island Quartet\, Tolling won two Gramm
 y Awards and earned a third nomination in 2015\, along with the 2016 DownB
 eat Critics Poll Rising Star Violin Award. He has performed with Chick Cor
 ea\, Ramsey Lewis\, Kenny Barron\, Paquito D'Rivera\, Leo Kottke and Sergi
 o & Odair Assad\, and is a current member of Bob Weir's Wolf Bros & Wolf P
 ack Band\, touring at venues including Red Rocks\, The Greek Theatre and R
 adio City Music Hall. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEv
 ent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/jean-luc-ponty-legacy-concert/9
 3473/
LOCATION:Berklee Performance Center\, Berklee Performance Center 136 Massa
 chusetts Avenue\, Boston\, MA\, 02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/jean-luc-ponty-legacy-concert/93473/
END:VEVENT
