BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet the Artist: From Iran | A Visual Testimony
DTSTART:20260930T000000
DTEND:20260930T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:df2678a5f16afa0cb73018b172ab57@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Azadeh Akhlaghi\, Visual Artist and Photographer In c
 onversation with Ilisa Barbash\, Curator of Visual Anthropology\, Peabody 
 Museum of Archaeology & Ethnology\, Harvard University From Iran: A Visual
  Testimony is a photography exhibition featuring Azadeh Akhlaghi’s stage
 d recreations of pivotal events in twentieth-century Iranian history. Thes
 e richly detailed tableaux span the years from 1908\, when the Shah dissol
 ved Iran’s first National Assembly\, to 1979\, when the monarchy was ove
 rthrown and the Islamic Republic was established. In this conversation\, A
 khlaghi will discuss how she selected\, reimagined\, and staged eleven inc
 idents from Iran’s tumultuous history\, drawing on archival research\, i
 nterviews\, and her background in cinema. She will also explore why these 
 events marked turning points in Iranian history and how they continue to s
 hape the country today. Presented by the Peabody Museum of Archaeology & E
 thnology and the Harvard Museums of Science & Culture. LEARN MORE / REGIST
 ER\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/m
 eet-the-artist%3a-from-iran-%7c-a-visual-testimony/93127/
LOCATION:Zoom\, Zoom
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/meet-the-artist%3a-from-iran-%7c-a-vi
 sual-testimony/93127/
END:VEVENT
