BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Living Declaration: When in the Course of Human Events
DTSTART:20260930T000000
DTEND:20260930T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:a286c46b25c979837d00d0c900d07c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Why do we have a Declaration of Independence? Why does it incl
 ude language about human rights? In conversation with MHS Chief Historian 
 Kanisorn Wongsrichanalai\, historian and former presidential speechwriter 
 Ted Widmer ( The Living Declaration ) explores the complex lineage of the 
 words and ideas in the Declaration and the dramatic sequence of events\, m
 any of them originating in Massachusetts\, that led to the creation of the
  most consequential state paper in history. Join us for a lively discussio
 n and the opportunity to view key MHS holdings like Thomas Jefferson's ori
 ginal manuscript copy of the Declaration. Featuring Ted Widmer\, historian
  and former presidential speechwriter\, in conversation with MHS Chief His
 torian Kanisorn Wongsrichanalai. This is a hybrid event in partnership wit
 h Library of America. The in-person reception starts at 5:00 and the progr
 am will begin 6:00 PM.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.me
 etboston.com/event/the-living-declaration%3a-when-in-the-course-of-human-e
 vents/93393/
LOCATION:Massachusetts Historical Society\, 1154 Boylston Street\, Boston
 \, MA\, 02215
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-living-declaration%3a-when-in-the
 -course-of-human-events/93393/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The NAA invites you to the 25th Annual Art Auction Exhibition & Ev
 ent
DTSTART:20260930T110000
DTEND:20261101T160000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:a8d4394a6b13fd4bbf9f41f327b5e1@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) invites artists\, members\, collectors\,
  friends\, and art lovers to gather for a celestial celebration of 25 year
 s of creativity\, connection\, and community. This year’s Art Auction ex
 hibition is on display from Wednesday\, September 2nd until Saturday\, Oct
 ober 3rd. A ticketed auction party will be held on Saturday\, October 3rd
 \, from 4-8pm. Over 160 artworks are available for online silent auction b
 idding now until October 3rd @6pm. In the downstairs Sargent Gallery\, the
  exhibit includes NAA Member Artwork featuring photography\, mixed media\,
  sculpture\, oil\, acrylic and more. Upstairs in the Hartson Gallery is th
 e Collector’s Collection – showcasing artwork donated from private col
 lections\, including work by notable artists such as Harold Feinstein\, Ca
 ra Weston\, and Carlos Mérida. For online bidding & tickets to our Octobe
 r 3rd party\, visit: Auctria.events./NewburyportArt25 Since 1948\, Newbury
 port Art has believed in the power of art to bring people together. For on
 e unforgettable event\, Saturday\, October 3rd\, from 4-8pm\, 65 Water Str
 eet will transform into a celebratory theme of a black\, white and silver 
 sky. The afternoon and evening offers a variety of ways to experience the 
 celebration including: live painting by Alan Bull and a chance to purchase
  his piece\; bidding on Members’ Artwork\, Collectors Collection\, and S
 ilent Auction Packages\; adding your own star and to an interactive commun
 ity constellation\; free tarot reading\; dancing to live jazz & swing with
  Jared Holaday\; sipping on a signature cocktail from the open bar\; enjoy
 ing catered food and dessert\; posing for your Moon Portrait in the sculpt
 ure garden\; and sharing your NAA story in an optional two-minute video in
 terview. NAA Member tickets: $70\; Non-member tickets: $90\; with a sugges
 ted attire of cosmic shine! Thank you to our lead sponsors\, Matter Commun
 ications\, Milestone 35 Tools & Woodworking\, and the Hylton Family Trust 
 for supporting our 25th Annual Art Auction. Gallery Hours: Wednesday throu
 gh Sunday from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More 
 information\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.
 org.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/ev
 ent/the-naa-invites-you-to-the-25th-annual-art-auction-exhibition-event/20
 26-09-30/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/the-naa-invites-you-to-the-25th-annual
 -art-auction-exhibition-event/2026-09-30/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Way We Never Were
DTSTART:20260930T000000
DTEND:20260930T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:9637b3f02a95949d521affeafa5b0a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:To celebrate our new exhibition The Way We Never Were: The Ame
 rican Professional Photographers Collection \, join us for a roundtable co
 nversation reflecting on Barbara Norfleet’s expansive influence on photo
 graphy at Harvard as a teacher\, curator\, and artist. Kiku Adatto\, Peter
  Galassi\, Lauren Greenfield\, and Susan Meiselas will share personal memo
 ries and talk about how Norfleet helped shape the study and practice of ph
 otography across generations. Following the lecture\, guests are invited t
 o visit the exhibition on Level 3. How to join: Register here. Fee: This i
 s a free event. Parking: Limited free parking available at Broadway Garage
 \, 7 Felton Street. Where to go: Enter on Broadway side of the building an
 d head to Menschel Hall. Accessibility accommodations: If you would like t
 o request accommodations for your visit\, please contact Visitor Services 
 at am_register@harvard.edu or 617-495-9400. For more details about accommo
 dations at the museums\, please see the Accessibility page. Speakers: Kiku
  Adatto\, Scholar-in-Residence at the Mahindra Humanities Center and Lectu
 rer on Social Studies\, Harvard University Peter Galassi\, Writer\, curato
 r\, and art historian Lauren Greenfield\, Artist\, documentary photographe
 r\, and documentary filmmaker Susan Meiselas\, Artist Audrey Sands\, Richa
 rd L. Menschel Associate Curator of Photography\, Harvard Art Museums\n\nS
 ources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-way-
 we-never-were/93384/
LOCATION:Harvard Art Museums\, 32 Quincy Street\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-way-we-never-were/93384/
END:VEVENT
