SUMMARY:MonoNeon's Micro-Southern Soul
DTSTART:20261001T000000
DTEND:20261001T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:3b12885aff166b40cf782a02d8a322@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Planet MicroJam Institute presents the Grammy Award–winn
 ing bassist MonoNeon performing original music and microtonal compositions
  with Berklee students and directed by David Fiuczynski. MonoNeon is a bas
 s virtuoso\, singer\, and songwriter from Memphis\, Tennessee\, known for 
 his imaginative approach to composition and improvisation. He was one of t
 he last musicians to work with Prince and received a Grammy Award for his 
 contributions to Nas's 2020 album King's Disease. In 2022\, Fender release
 d the MonoNeon Jazz Bass V as part of the MonoNeon Capsule Collection. Thr
 oughout his career\, MonoNeon has collaborated with artists including Mavi
 s Staples\, George Clinton\, Pete Rock\, Ne-Yo\, Mac Miller\, Georgia Anne
  Muldrow\, and Ghost-Note\, and has appeared at festivals such as the Newp
 ort Jazz Festival\, Montreal Jazz Festival\, and Melbourne International J
 azz Festival. This performance highlights his original music and explores 
 microtonal composition through collaboration with Berklee students. LEARN 
 MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetbo
 ston.com/event/mononeons-micro-southern-soul/93472/
LOCATION:Berklee Performance Center\, Berklee Performance Center 136 Massa
 chusetts Avenue\, Boston\, MA\, 02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/mononeons-micro-southern-soul/93472/
END:VEVENT
