BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boston Landmarks Orchestra: “Celebration of National Hispanic He
 ritage Month”
DTSTART:20261002T000000
DTEND:20261002T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:cce3e00e9f2ca1efd7b80f73ed8238@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Boston Landmarks Orchestra\, led by Music Director Christopher
  Wilkins\, will present a free community concert\, “A Celebration of Nat
 ional Hispanic Heritage Month\,” on Friday\, October 2 at 7:00pm at Chel
 sea High School. The concert will bring professional musicians and student
 s from Chelsea High School Orchestra together for an evening of orchestral
  music celebrating Hispanic and Latin American cultural traditions. The pr
 ogram features music by composers from across the Americas and Europe\, in
 cluding Arturo Márquez’s vibrant Danzón No. 2\, Louis Moreau Gottschal
 k’s Souvenir de Porto Rico\, and Aaron Copland’s Paisaje Mexicana and 
 Danza de Jalisco from Three Latin-American Sketches. The program also incl
 udes works by Wolfgang Amadè Mozart\, Ottorino Respighi\, Leroy Anderson
 \, and Benjamin Britten/Gioachino Rossini. The evening will also include f
 ood and refreshments following the performance. “This concert reflects o
 ur mission to build community through great music\,” says Music Director
  Christopher Wilkins. “By performing in Boston-area neighborhoods like C
 helsea\, we make live orchestral music accessible to everyone while celebr
 ating cultural traditions that resonate deeply with our audiences. Perform
 ing alongside students makes the experience especially meaningful. It give
 s young musicians the opportunity to share the stage with professional art
 ists and be part of a larger musical community.” For more information an
 d to RSVP\, visit landmarksorchestra.org. Boston Landmarks Orchestra: “C
 elebration of National Hispanic Heritage Month” Friday\, October 2 at 7:
 00 pm Chelsea High School\, 299 Everett Avenue\, Chelsea\, MA 02150 Ticket
 s: Free with RSVP Boston Landmarks Orchestra | Christopher Wilkins\, condu
 ctor Students from Chelsea High School Orchestra\, Ali You\, director Prog
 ram to include: Wolfgang Amadè Mozart - Eine Kleine Nachtmusik (excerpt) 
 Arturo Márquez - Danzon No. 2 Ottorino Respighi - Serenata for small orch
 estra Louis Moreau Gottschalk arr. David Kempers - Souvenir de Porto Rico 
 Leroy Anderson - Jazz Pizzicato—Jazz Legato Aaron Copland - Paisaje Mexi
 cana & Danza de Jalisco from Three Latin-American Sketches Britten/Rossini
  - Soirées Musicales MORE INFO / RSVP\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page
 : https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston-landmarks-orchestra%3a-%e2%80%9c
 celebration-of-national-hispanic-heritage-month%e2%80%9d/92906/
LOCATION:Chelsea High School\, Chelsea High School 299 Everett Avenue\, Ch
 elsea\, MA\, 02150
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston-landmarks-orchestra%3a-%e2%80%
 9ccelebration-of-national-hispanic-heritage-month%e2%80%9d/92906/
END:VEVENT
