 workshop at the Osterville Village Library. Designed for artists of all sk
 ill levels\, this hands-on program offers participants the opportunity to 
 explore the fundamentals of drawing while developing their own creative vo
 ice. Through guided exercises and personalized instruction\, Jim will intr
 oduce key techniques such as observation\, composition\, shading\, and lin
 e work. Participants will work with a variety of subjects and materials\, 
 gaining confidence and expanding their artistic skills in a supportive and
  welcoming environment. Whether you’re picking up a pencil for the first
  time or looking to refine your practice\, this workshop is a perfect way 
 to spark creativity\, connect with others\, and enjoy the art of drawing i
 n a beautiful community setting. All ages and abilities welcome. Friday Oc
 tober 2nd at 3:30pm in the Anne Williams McGraw Atrium at the Osterville V
 illage Library. For more information or to register for this event\, pleas
 e contact Amy Wolfe at awolfe@clamsnet.org or by calling the OVL directly 
