BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:US & UK Summit on Race: Honouring Excellence\, Defending Democracy
DTSTART:20261002T000000
DTEND:20261002T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:87bc64fa54a6ad498c685c0c1cc9de@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Every October\, Black History Month in the United Kingdom invi
 tes us to celebrate Black achievement\, learn from history\, and consider 
 the work that lies ahead. This year\, the US & UK Summit on Race will begi
 n the month with a virtual gathering that brings voices from both sides of
  the Atlantic into conversation. Join us on Friday\, October 2\, 2026\, fo
 r Honouring Excellence\, Defending Democracy: A Transatlantic Conversation
  on Race\, Power and Justice. The Summit will explore how communities buil
 d influence\, how institutions respond to calls for change\, and why publi
 c participation matters. It is an opportunity to listen\, reflect\, and en
 gage with ideas that connect experiences in the United Kingdom and the Uni
 ted States. Our keynote speaker\, Lee Jasper of the United Kingdom\, has s
 pent more than four decades working in civil rights\, community organizing
 \, and public policy. He was a founding chair of Operation Black Vote and 
 served as Director of Policing and Equalities to the Mayor of London. Toda
 y\, he chairs the Alliance for Police Accountability. His experience in bo
 th community advocacy and government will bring a valuable perspective to 
 the Summit’s discussion of race\, power\, and accountability. Featured p
 anelist Dr. Georgianna Meléndez of the United States is an Assistant Prof
 essor of Management at Western New England University and a former Assista
 nt Chancellor for Diversity\, Equity\, and Inclusion at the University of 
 Massachusetts Boston. Her research examines structural bias\, discriminati
 on within organizations\, and organizational behavior. She has also led no
 nprofit and statewide initiatives to expand opportunity and representation
 . She brings an academic and practical perspective to the conversation. US
  UK Summit Co-Founder Dr. Garth Dallas will moderate the conversations and
  engage in a spirited discussion with featured panelist Dr. Meléndez. Bla
 ck History Month is a time to honour the people whose leadership and contr
 ibutions have shaped our world. It is also a time to ask what we can learn
  from their work as we face the questions of our own day. We hope you will
  be part of this conversation across borders. KEYNOTE SPEAKER Lee Jasper (
 United Kingdom) DISTINGUISHED PANEL SPEAKERS Dr. Georgianna Meléndez (Uni
 ted States) Dr. Garth Dallas (United Kingdom) Why Attend? Dive into a thou
 ght-provoking dialogue that connects the historical past to today’s chal
 lenges and tomorrow’s opportunities. Whether you’re a student\, profes
 sional\, activist\, or lifelong learner\, this event is your opportunity t
 o gain fresh perspectives and actionable insights from leaders at the fore
 front of the racial equity movement. HOSTED BY THE US UK SUMMIT ON RACE FO
 UNDERS Carole Copeland Thomas (United States) Garth Dallas (United Kingdom
 ) Bill Wells (United States) What to Expect Engaging discussions with worl
 d-class keynote speakers. Deep insights into the past\, present\, and futu
 re of racial equity. Opportunities to reflect and connect with a global au
 dience. Invite a Friend or Colleague! This event is free and open to all. 
 Share the invitation and be part of a global community committed to unders
 tanding why race matters —each and every month. Pre-Register Today Visit
  www.usukrace.com for complete details.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent pag
 e: https://www.meetboston.com/event/us-%26-uk-summit-on-race%3a-honouring-
 excellence-defending-democracy/93485/
LOCATION:Online\, Online Event\, Boston\, MA
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/us-%26-uk-summit-on-race%3a-honouring
 -excellence-defending-democracy/93485/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261002T111500
DTEND:20261002T161500
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:890c1aca1fbe595bfab3cefcb252f9@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-10-02/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 0-02/
END:VEVENT
