SUMMARY:Woods Hole Film Festival Dinner & A Movie: WBCN and the American R
 evolution
DTSTART:20261003T000000
DTEND:20261003T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:f5cb5496e244d4afa777a331fd7da2@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The amazing\, untold story of the radical underground radio st
 ation WBCN-FM\, set against the dazzling and profound social\, political\,
  and cultural changes that took place in Boston and nationally during the 
 late-1960s and early-70s. Told through the actual sights\, sounds\, and st
 ories of a compelling cast of characters who connected through the radio s
 tation\, exploding music and countercultural scenes\, militant anti-war ac
 tivism\, civil rights struggles\, and the emerging women’s and LGBTQ-lib
 eration movements. It's "the incredible\, true story of how a radio statio
 n\, politics\, and rock ‘n’ roll changed everything." More information
  and tickets HERE. DINNER & A MOVIE is a film series presented by Woods Ho
 le Film Festival as part of its year-round independent film program\, feat
 uring twice-monthly screenings of independent films from early fall to lat
 e spring. The Dinner and a Movie series includes films from the Woods Hole
  Film Festival\, as well as independent films curated specifically for the
  series. ABOUT THE SCREENINGS: Dinner and a Movie screenings are held at t
 he Woods Hole Oceanographic Institution’s Redfield Auditorium. Screening
 s typically begin at 7:00 pm\, with doors opening for seating thirty minut
 es prior. Redfield Auditorium is located at 45 Water Street in Woods Hole.
  The facility is wheelchair accessible. Hearing assistance devices are ava
 ilable at the venue\, upon request. Street parking is available in Woods H
 ole. Free parking is available in certain lots operated by the Woods Hole 
 Oceanographic Institution after 5 pm. ABOUT THE DINNER: Ticketholders rece
 ive a discount at the Captain Kidd Restaurant & Quahog Republic Leeside Pu
 b. Reservations are encouraged. The Captain Kidd Restaurant at 77 Water St
 reet offers Dinner and a Movie ticket holders a 10% discount on the meal p
 ortion (excluding any alcohol) of their bill. For reservations for parties
  up to eight people\, please complete the online reservation form and in t
 he “special request” field\, please indicate Dinner and a Movie. This 
 will help the staff accommodate the timing for the screening start. For pa
 rties of nine or more\, please call 508-548-8563. Please note: The Captain
  Kidd restaurant is closed seasonally from late December\, 2026 until late
  April\, 2027.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capec
 odchamber.org/event/woods-hole-film-festival-dinner-%26-a-movie%3a-wbcn-an
 d-the-american-revolution/52387/
LOCATION:Woods Hole Film Festival\, Inc.\, Redfield Auditorium at WHOI Wat
 er Street\, Woods Hole\, MA\, 02543
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/woods-hole-film-festival-dinner-%
 26-a-movie%3a-wbcn-and-the-american-revolution/52387/
END:VEVENT
