BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Siqing Lu Violin Recital
DTSTART:20261004T000000
DTEND:20261004T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:644a0c16cc6962a48c318c34f97f39@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate America’s 250th anniversary with an extraordinary 
 evening of music at one of Boston’s most historic landmarks. On October 
 4\, 2026\, internationally acclaimed violinist Siqing Lu joins pianist Der
 ek Wang at Faneuil Hall for East Meets West: From Mozart and Beethoven to 
 The Butterfly Lovers\, a special recital bringing together masterpieces of
  Western classical music and one of China’s most beloved musical works. 
 The program begins with Mozart’s elegant Violin Sonata No. 10 in B-flat 
 Major\, K. 378\, followed by Beethoven’s dramatic Violin Sonata No. 7 in
  C Minor\, Op. 30\, No. 2. The second half features a complete performance
  of The Butterfly Lovers Violin Concerto\, the celebrated Chinese work ins
 pired by the legendary story of Liang Shanbo and Zhu Yingtai. Siqing Lu is
  the first Asian violinist to win First Prize at Italy’s prestigious Pag
 anini International Violin Competition. He has performed in more than 40 c
 ountries and at renowned venues including Lincoln Center\, Vienna’s Musi
 kverein\, London’s Royal Opera House\, and the National Centre for the P
 erforming Arts in Beijing. Presented at Faneuil Hall—Boston’s historic
  “Cradle of Liberty”—the concert marks America’s 250th anniversary
  through a musical dialogue across cultures\, generations\, and traditions
 . LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://ww
 w.meetboston.com/event/siqing-lu-violin-recital/92595/
LOCATION:Faneuil Hall\, Faneuil Hall 4 South Market Street\, Boston\, MA\,
  02109
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/siqing-lu-violin-recital/92595/
END:VEVENT
