BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261008T111500
DTEND:20261008T161500
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:a463d23682fbc1ff0615fc712a4848@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-10-08/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 0-08/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Night At The Movies 2026 - Chatham
DTSTART:20261009T000000
DTEND:20261009T000000
DTSTAMP:20260928T185823Z
UID:595f8a5f659f55bc9381349f7f3592@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Cape Cod Music Society is delighted to invite you to a spe
 cial performance of "A Night At The Movies" on Friday\, October 9\, 2026\,
  at 7:00 p.m. at the beautiful St. Christopher's Church in Chatham. Follow
 ing the success of our summer concerts\, we're bringing this exciting prod
 uction to Chatham for one unforgettable evening. Featuring the Cape Cod St
 ring Quartet\, two pianists\, bass guitar\, drums\, three outstanding voca
 lists\, and an all-star lineup of guest musicians\, this concert is inspir
 ed by the energy and excitement of a classic "Pops" performance and promis
 es an unforgettable musical experience. Featured performers include Dan Fl
 onta\, Jeff Pearson\, Sofia Nikas\, Nancy Torrente\, Emma Fahle\, Anna McE
 ntee\, Cameron Phillips\, Bart Weisman\, Eric Williams\, Jonathan Weir\, a
 nd James Peterson. Audiences will enjoy an evening of beloved music from f
 ilm\, television\, Broadway\, and pop classics\, including favorites from 
 ABBA\, Bohemian Rhapsody\, Skyfall\, The Lion King\, Cinema Paradiso\, Moo
 n River\, Les Misérables\, Jaws\, Pirates of the Caribbean\, The Bodyguar
 d\, Dirty Dancing\, Top Gun\, Rocky\, and many more. Whether you're a movi
 e lover\, Broadway enthusiast\, or simply enjoy outstanding live music\, t
 his concert offers something for everyone. From soaring vocal performances
  and thrilling instrumental arrangements to timeless cinematic themes\, "A
  Night At The Movies" is a celebration of music that has inspired generati
 ons. This concert continues the Cape Cod Music Society's mission of bringi
 ng exceptional live performances to our community while supporting music e
 ducation and creating opportunities for young musicians throughout the reg
 ion. Concert Details Friday\, October 9\, 2026 7:00 p.m. St. Christopher's
  Church 625 Main Street Chatham\, MA Tickets: $45 General Admission Advanc
 e registration is recommended\, as seating is limited. Reserve your seats 
 today: https://www.capecodmusicsociety.org/event-details/a-night-at-the-mo
 vies-2026-chatham-fourth-annual-concert-series Gather your family and frie
 nds and join us for an unforgettable evening filled with spectacular music
 \, extraordinary performers\, and the magic of the movies. We look forward
  to seeing you in Chatham! Warmly\, Dan Flonta President\, Cape Cod Music 
 Society Founder & First Violin\, Cape Cod String Quartet Concert Trailer: 
 https://youtu.be/9-wfXVjwkAw\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: htt
 ps://www.capecodchamber.org/event/a-night-at-the-movies-2026-chatham/52170
 /
LOCATION:St. Christopher's Church\, 625 Main Street\, Chatham\, MA\, 02633
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/a-night-at-the-movies-2026-chatha
 m/52170/
END:VEVENT
